{"w":2400,"lines":[{"t":"Test 3","h":0.014322443199382362,"c":1,"w":0.058153603871663434,"x":0.13347463829164538,"y":0.10112366181304444},{"x":0.45679012265097146,"y":0.14534883706636936,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.12962963104248043,"t":"READING"},{"x":0.13374485429436325,"w":0.28806584676106772,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","c":1,"h":0.016020900088288825,"y":0.20200235586354853},{"c":1,"x":0.13374486631274277,"y":0.23546511611771725,"w":0.76543207804361979,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","h":0.017479524735988683},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.25436046495970843,"x":0.13374485497921693,"w":0.15843621571858721,"t":"Passage 1 below.","c":1},{"y":0.28916372225414566,"h":0.020429301177655068,"x":0.37242798720381626,"w":0.3086419677734375,"c":1,"t":"Henry Moore (1898-1986)"},{"y":0.32267441880754344,"h":0.018903908656539348,"c":1,"w":0.56378601074218748,"t":"The British sculptor Henry Moore was a leading figure","x":0.24279835713919415},{"y":0.34010600695603888,"h":0.018905620552485347,"t":"in the 20th-century art world","c":1,"x":0.37448559315202234,"w":0.30041152954101558},{"y":0.37441174109704833,"t":"Henry Moore was born in Castleford, a small town near Leeds in the north of England. He","w":0.72439244588216145,"h":0.018148719913406275,"c":1,"x":0.13368742024306432},{"h":0.018134181154069173,"w":0.74093724568684893,"t":"was the seventh child of Raymond Moore and his wife Mary Baker. He studied at Castleford","c":1,"x":0.13364827414118394,"y":0.39084312815009326},{"t":"Grammar School from 1909 to 1915, where his early interest in art was encouraged by his teacher","c":1,"h":0.019207991475351349,"x":0.13367545823890187,"w":0.78410685221354171,"y":0.4075532739783867},{"h":0.018246402448422794,"c":1,"y":0.42434075864218657,"t":"Alice Gostick. After leaving school, Moore hoped to become a sculptor, but instead he complied","w":0.77174357096354163,"x":0.13368083235497827},{"y":0.44186046497610143,"h":0.014558851648696858,"t":"with his father's wish that he train as a schoolteacher. He had to abandon his training in 1917","w":0.74485595703124985,"c":1,"x":0.13168724810339172},{"y":0.45930232542939131,"w":0.47325103759765624,"c":1,"t":"when he was sent to France to fight in the First World War.","h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.13168723841353475},{"y":0.49087621273687021,"x":0.13368007365897122,"c":1,"t":"After the war, Moore enrolled at the Leeds School of Art, where he studied for two years. In his","w":0.76556111653645842,"h":0.018125178535919662},{"h":0.018113362073055916,"t":"first year, he spent most of his time drawing. Although he wanted to study sculpture, no teacher","w":0.76554494222005198,"y":0.50824482650536529,"x":0.13163721585808313,"c":1},{"w":0.77172805786132814,"c":1,"y":0.52446274051897268,"h":0.017851047156415834,"t":"was appointed until his second year. At the end of that year, he passed the sculpture examination","x":0.13367935994206087},{"c":1,"x":0.13168724686941366,"h":0.016031172025610885,"t":"and was awarded a scholarship to the Royal College of Art in London. In September 1921, he","y":0.54210836299748888,"w":0.75102879842122394},{"x":0.13168724771850321,"t":"moved to London and began three years of advanced study in sculpture.","w":0.57818929036458333,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"y":0.55948174313247934},{"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1,"x":0.13374485906597366,"t":"Alongside the instruction he received at the Royal College, Moore visited many of the London","y":0.59156976728110333,"w":0.75720163981119792},{"t":"museums, particularly the British Museum, which had a wide-ranging collection of ancient","w":0.73270985921223963,"h":0.019991502885402856,"x":0.13159493668835343,"y":0.60646178542671692,"c":1},{"x":0.13160063310234998,"y":0.62360679683956666,"c":1,"t":"sculpture. During these visits, he discovered the power and beauty of ancient Egyptian and","w":0.72653900146484385,"h":0.01972358443009703},{"y":0.63862877317578659,"h":0.02130609519068849,"t":"African sculpture. As he became increasingly interested in theseiprimitive forms of art, he","w":0.73273381551106764,"c":1,"x":0.13362954310824507},{"w":0.39711934407552085,"x":0.13374485461098515,"t":"turned away from European sculptural traditions.","h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.65988372078139812,"c":1},{"h":0.018524537238131078,"x":0.13365924336506027,"c":1,"y":0.69011635893922085,"t":"After graduating, Moore spent the first six months of 1925 travelling in France. When he visited","w":0.77177973429361968},{"t":"the Trocadero Museum in Paris, he was impressed by a cast of a Mayan* sculpture of the rain","w":0.74513997395833331,"h":0.024567490612519727,"x":0.13359239602964484,"c":1,"y":0.70256684011357828},{"y":0.72526501740289573,"h":0.016014052504504606,"x":0.13374485531043356,"t":"spirit. It was a male reclining figure with its knees drawn up together, and its head at a right angle","c":1,"w":0.78189300537109374},{"y":0.74070912735372929,"t":"to its body. Moore became fascinated with this stone sculpture, which he thought had a power","x":0.13367254276214549,"w":0.75117802937825517,"h":0.019413924469964705,"c":1},{"y":0.75703751742188874,"h":0.019125135262245574,"c":1,"w":0.7553650410970052,"t":"and originality that no other stone sculpture possessed. He himself started carving a variety of","x":0.13365085750201483},{"t":"subjects in stone, including depictions of reclining women, mother-and-child groups, and masks.","x":0.13374486440952865,"c":1,"y":0.77470930271245464,"h":0.01889534805351778,"w":0.77777776082356764},{"w":0.75720163981119781,"c":1,"x":0.1337448591080091,"t":"Moore's exceptional talent soon gained recognition, and in 1926 he started work as a sculpture","y":0.80800942278020027,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"t":"instructor at the Royal College. In 1933, he became a member of a group of young artists called","y":0.82339832629869181,"w":0.77172993977864601,"h":0.020552903659492583,"x":0.13163769240542014,"c":1},{"y":0.8399868593477714,"t":"Unit One. The aim of the group was to convince the English public of the merits of the emerging","x":0.13367619030461356,"c":1,"w":0.77588602701822917,"h":0.019874745740766975},{"h":0.015843684597487195,"t":"international movement in modern art and architecture.","w":0.446685791015625,"y":0.85774415812597449,"x":0.13365709253224622,"c":1},{"x":0.13786007005262887,"y":0.89811542995360882,"h":0.011778563015312216,"t":"Mayan: belonging to an ancient civilisation that inhabited parts of current-day Mexico, Guatemala, Belize, El Salvador and Honduras.","c":1,"w":0.74691360473632806},{"x":0.13374485607959105,"y":0.92005813935786906,"t":"58","h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"w":0.024691357612609877}],"h":3395}